@startuml
title Returning equipment with reported faults
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
participant ":LabLog" as App
participant ":ReturnCommands" as Returns
participant ":Inventory" as Inventory
participant ":LoanBook" as Loans
participant "loan:Loan" as Loan

[-> App : return OSC-001 faults/Damaged cable
activate App
App -> Returns : execute(input)
activate Returns
note right of Returns : Validate syntax and optional faults field
Returns -> Inventory : getEquipmentUnits()
activate Inventory
Inventory --> Returns : equipment units
deactivate Inventory
note right of Returns : Check that the asset exists
Returns -> Loans : getLoans()
activate Loans
Loans --> Returns : loan records
deactivate Loans
note right of Returns
Filter by asset ID and active state.
Require exactly one active loan.
today = LocalDate.now(clock)
end note
Returns -> Loan : markReturned(today, faults)
activate Loan
note right of Loan
Validate active state, date and fault text
before assigning either return field.
end note
Loan --> Returns
deactivate Loan
Returns --> App : confirmation text
deactivate Returns
ref over App : In persistent sessions, save changes before displaying success
App -->[ : display confirmation
deactivate App
legend bottom
Successful path shown; individual accessor calls are omitted.
Validation errors propagate to LabLog, which displays an error.
endlegend
@enduml
